          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.086,
            0.764,
            0.105
          ],
          "content": "d. A quadrilateral with reflection symmetry but not having rotational symmetry"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.191,
            0.119,
            0.45,
            0.292
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_38_image_1.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.33,
            0.883,
            0.366
          ],
          "content": "**Q4. In a figure,** $\\mathbf { 6 0 ^ { \\circ } }$ **is the smallest angle of symmetry. What are the other angles of symmetry of the figure?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.375,
            0.65,
            0.393
          ],
          "content": "**Ans.** Other angles of symmetry = 120°, 180°, 240°, 300°, 360°."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.429,
            0.881,
            0.465
          ],
          "content": "**Q5. In the figure, 60° in an angle of symmetry. The figure has two angles of symmetry less then 60°. What is its smallest angle of symmetry?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.474,
            0.493,
            0.493
          ],
          "content": "**Ans.** The smallest angle of symmetry $= 2 0 ^ { \\circ }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.528,
            0.88,
            0.601
          ],
          "content": "**Q6. Can we have a figure with rotational symmetry whose smallest angle of symmetry is** a. $4 5 ^ { \\circ } ?$ b. $1 7 ^ { \\circ } ?$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.611,
            0.493,
            0.656
          ],
          "content": "**Ans.** a. yes, as $3 6 0 ^ { \\circ }$ is a multiple of $4 5 ^ { \\circ }$ b. $\\mathrm { { N o } , }$ as $3 6 0 ^ { \\circ }$ is not a multiple of $1 7 ^ { \\circ } ,$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.691,
            0.65,
            0.71
          ],
          "content": "**Q7. This is a picture of the new Parliament Building in Delhi.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.162,
            0.719,
            0.882,
            0.755
          ],
          "content": "**a. Does the outer boundary of the picture have reflection symmetry? If so, draw the lines of symmetries. How many are they?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.162,
            0.764,
            0.884,
            0.799
          ],
          "content": "**b. Does it have rotational symmetry around its centre? If so, find the angles of rotational symmetry.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.808,
            0.883,
            0.872
          ],
          "content": "**Ans.** a. Yes, the outer boundary of the picture has 3 lines of symmetry. b. Yes, the outer boundary has rotational symmetry. The angles of rotational symmetry are 120°, 240°, 360°."
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.482,
            0.927,
            0.517,
            0.942
          ],
          "content": "[14]"
        }
      ]
    }
